compliment!), and I'm still not sure what to make of this. But it seems to=
=20
me that {ti blanu je zdani} is *not* a good example sentence in the=20
reference grammar.


 (Since 'the x2 of a one-place brivla' is a separate issue, separately=20
discussed, that need not distract us here, I'll stick to the {sutra je=20
jipci} example.)


 la gejyspa ku cusku di'e

> "mi sutra je jipci" is a perfectly fine sentence to say


 I agree that 'I am fast, and a chicken' is what that sentence is probably=
=20
supposed to mean, and what will be understood by a co-operative listener.=
=20
But then, the speaker should have said {mi sutra gi'e jipci} or so. I don't=
=20
think {mi sutra je jipci} makes sense. If it did, that would mean that=20
places could be pragmatically cancelled out/filled with {zi'o} =85 or {no=
=20
da}, whatever. But I think a legitimate Lojbanic reaction (besides {ki'a})=
=20
to {mi sutra je jipci} would always be {sutra je jipci ma}=97the second=20
argument is still there and can always be made explicit. Otherwise, we'd=20
end up with place structure ambiguity in ellipsis sentences, wouldn't we?


 My tentative conclusion is that CLL #12.12 might better be listed as an=20
erratum. Opinions?

